From: ghidra_rh850 project
Subject: [PATCH] v850: omit saved-register frames for optimized non-returning functions

The V850 prologue reserves space for, and saves, every call-saved
register a function touches plus the link pointer, even when the
function is known never to return. Permanent firmware loops (for
example the TSS3 request signer foreground resident) then pay prologue
code and stack for incoming register values that no caller and no
unwinder can ever consume.

Skip the saved-register scan in compute_register_save_size for ordinary
functions declared not to return, but only when optimization is enabled
and no consumer of the saved state can exist: exception handling off
and neither synchronous nor asynchronous unwind tables requested.
Locals, spills and outgoing argument areas are accounted outside this
function, so genuine stack needs survive. Interrupt handlers take the
earlier branch of the same function and keep their complete
architectural saves, and every returning function keeps its saves,
so the change is invisible to the ordinary ABI.

Keep this local patch until equivalent support lands upstream.

Pinned base: GCC 78d4ac73dd391005b895a6148cd9831e28e1208b.
---
 gcc/config/v850/v850.cc | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/gcc/config/v850/v850.cc b/gcc/config/v850/v850.cc
--- a/gcc/config/v850/v850.cc
+++ b/gcc/config/v850/v850.cc
@@ -1460,7 +1460,14 @@ compute_register_save_size (long * p_reg_saved)
 	    break;
 	  }
     }
-  else
+  /* A non-returning ordinary function needs no incoming register values
+     when neither exception handling nor stack unwinding can consume them.
+     Interrupt handlers above retain their complete architectural saves.  */
+  else if (!(optimize > 0
+	     && TREE_THIS_VOLATILE (current_function_decl)
+	     && !flag_exceptions
+	     && !flag_unwind_tables
+	     && !flag_asynchronous_unwind_tables))
     {
       /* Find the first register that needs to be saved.  */
       for (i = 0; i <= 31; i++)
